2026-05-27 10:34:31,664 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative activities. Our solution leverages a sovereign large language model (Mistral 7B Instruct) for content drafting and suggestion of actions, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities for search within administrative documents, and integrates with existing systems via API gateways like Kong or Apigee. Ensuring compliance with GDPR, EU AI Act, and data sovereignty requirements, we host the solution on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU. Our approach balances performance, explicability, and environmental sustainability, aiming for 99.9% availability, response times under 2 seconds, and a significant reduction in energy consumption through digital sobriety practices.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution to improve the efficiency of its administrative services and quality of service rendered to users. The expected solution must provide intelligent assistance tools for municipal agents, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. It must integrate into existing practices without disrupting current work modes. Key requirements include compliance with regulatory frameworks (GDPR, EU AI Act), data sovereignty, high availability, low response times, explicability of recommendations, and environmental sustainability.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution is built around the Mistral 7B Instruct large language model, fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus to enhance accuracy in administrative content drafting and suggestion of actions. The RAG capabilities, employing Dense vector semantic search and BM25 sparse search strategies, enable efficient search within administrative documents and knowledge bases stored in vector stores like Qdrant and Weaviate.

For hosting, we utilize SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure provided by partners like Outscale or OVHcloud, ensuring data residency within the EU and compliance with GDPR requirements. Our standard data protection agreement template version 3.2 and intellectual property policy confirm that all client data remains the sole property of the contracting authority.

To achieve high availability (99.9%) and low response times (<2 seconds), we leverage expertise in containerization using Docker and Kubernetes, along with monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana. Integration with existing systems is facilitated through API gateways and message brokers such as Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ.

Security and compliance are ensured through access control standards (multi-factor authentication, role-based access control), AI security controls (output PII redaction, confidence threshold escalation), and a review process for recommendations or proposals issued by the solution. Our legal basis for GDPR compliance is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest.

The global budget for the project over 4 years is estimated at 3 million euros, with our target gross margin percentage being 28%. This translates to a projected margin of 840,000 euros. Cost optimization strategies include renegotiation with subcontractors and potential scope adjustments.

For environmental sustainability, we implement digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation (reducing GPU energy by approximately 40%), auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching (estimating a 20% recompute reduction), and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy. Our partnership with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, using 100% renewable energy and having ISO14001 certification, further minimizes the environmental footprint.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements specified in the tender have been left unaddressed by our proposal. Each aspect, from technical architecture to legal compliance, security, budget, innovation strategy, and sustainability, has been carefully considered and integrated into our proposed solution.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its specialized partners, is committed to delivering a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that meets the City of Belval's needs for enhancing administrative efficiency and user service quality. By leveraging cutting-edge technologies, ensuring regulatory compliance, and prioritizing environmental sustainability, we aim to establish a long-term partnership that supports the city's digital transformation strategy while respecting its budgetary constraints and commitment to innovation.
